tasqx mcp: serving over stdio (scope=write)
{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"tools":{}},"instructions":"tasqx is this workspace's organiser: its backlog, and its long-term memory, one searchable index over imported knowledge docs and the annotations written on tasks. Use it instead of an in-conversation todo list or a memory file.\n\nSearch first. Call tasqx_search_memory before resuming work, choosing between designs, touching a convention-bearing file, or asserting how this project does something. Query with two or three keywords, never a sentence: every word is required, and `matched` shows what ran. Try a second wording before concluding nothing is there. A hit is a snippet: read a doc whole with tasqx_get_memory, and an annotation (source `task:#<id>`) with tasqx_get_task.\n\nTrack multi-step work as tasks. Anything with more than one step, or that could outlive this session, goes in the backlog: tasqx_list_projects before tasqx_create_project, tasqx_add_task per piece, tasqx_add_dependency to order them, tasqx_add_check for acceptance criteria. Pick work with tasqx_list_tasks and the filter `@working`; blocked and waiting tasks are hidden there by design. Per task: tasqx_brief_task, then tasqx_start_timer, do the work, tasqx_annotate_task with what was decided and delivered, and tasqx_complete_task naming in checks_passed what you proved. Obsolete work is cancelled with tasqx_cancel_task, never left open.\n\nWrite as you go. Only annotation bodies are indexed, never titles, so name files and symbols in them. Call tasqx_add_memory when a decision settles or you learn a convention written down nowhere: the ruling in the first line, the why under it, the path in source. A wrong entry is removed with tasqx_remove_memory (permanent), not corrected beside.\n\nAn empty store is a store nobody seeded. If searches keep returning nothing, ask the user to run `tasqx memory import <docs-dir>` once per markdown folder; no MCP tool imports. The CLI is always `tasqx <verb>`: a bare `tasqx` opens a full-screen dashboard and hangs a tool call. Tool descriptions here are deliberately short and state only the contract; the reasoning behind a rule is in DESIGN.md §12 under the D-number the description cites, which tasqx_search_memory finds once those docs are imported (D155).\n\nNo code mapper on PATH: tell the user once that `tasqx setup` shows how to install ripwire.\n\nRecent notes for project website (context, not rulings):\n- pricing-page-decisions: # Pricing page Three tiers, annual billing shown first. The release of v2 waits for legal to sign off the new terms.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","serverInfo":{"name":"tasqx","version":"0.12.0"}}}
{"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"tools":[{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_list_tasks"},"description":"List tasks matching a filter-DSL query — the CLI's grammar, e.g. \"project:work status:pending +api due.before:tomorrow\". Paged: the response carries `count`, `total` and `next_offset`, null once nothing is left. Rows carry a default field set unless you name `fields` (D152).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"fields":{"description":"Restrict each row to these fields. Omit for short_id, title, status, priority, urgency, blocked, due, project, tags, with null-valued keys dropped; send [] for the whole row.","items":{"enum":["_rev","active_since","blocked","budget_tokens","completed","created","depends_on","due","estimate","id","modified","priority","project","recurrence","remind","scheduled","short_id","status","status_unrecognized","tags","title","tokens","tracked","tracked_adjustment","urgency","wait"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"filter":{"description":"Filter DSL, e.g. \"status:pending +api\". \"@working\" is the actionable set. Omit it (or send \"\") for every task.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Rows to return. Omit for this tool's page (100), shrunk to fit the response byte budget; a named limit is honoured up to 10000.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"Matching rows to skip; pass the previous `next_offset`. Ordering is stable across pages.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"sort":{"description":"Sort keys, e.g. [\"-urgency\", \"due\"]; \"-\" descends. Valid: urgency, short_id, priority, due, created, modified, title, tokens, estimate, tracked. An unknown key is rejected.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_list_tasks"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_get_task"},"description":"Get one task's full detail: fields, tags, annotations, dependencies. Annotations come back in pages counted from the newest, oldest first within a page — the response carries `annotations_total`, and `annotations_next_offset` whenever older ones were left out.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"annotations_limit":{"description":"Most-recent annotations to return; omit for this tool's page (20). An over-budget page is cut to what fits and the view names the `annotations_offset` for the rest; `include_json: true` spends that budget first. 0 returns none.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"annotations_offset":{"description":"Annotations to skip, counted back from the newest; pass the previous `annotations_next_offset`.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"explain":{"description":"Add `urgency_breakdown` (`priority`, `due_proximity`, `age`, `total`) — the terms `urgency` sums (D1). Default false.","type":"boolean"},"include_json":{"description":"Send the machine-readable JSON block beside the rendered view. Default FALSE: it is one result twice and you read the view (D151). True when a SCRIPT parses this.","type":"boolean"},"max_body_bytes":{"description":"Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"view":{"description":"How the rendered block is spelled. Default \"markdown\", the view YOU read; \"card\" is the D146 72-column box card in a text fence, for a PERSON deciding on the task (D164), and quotes only the first annotation.","enum":["markdown","card"],"type":"string"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_get_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_brief_task"},"description":"Everything you need before starting one task, in ONE call (D136): the task, the tasks it depends on with what each of THEM concluded, what it blocks, and memory found under a query tasqx derives from the task's title, tags and project. Use tasqx_get_task when you only need the task.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_json":{"description":"Send the machine-readable JSON block beside the rendered view. Default FALSE: it is the brief again, snippets included (D151). True when a script parses this.","type":"boolean"},"include_rank":{"description":"Add the raw FTS5 bm25 `rank` to each memory hit; default false, and visible only in the `include_json` block. LOWER is the better match and hits arrive sorted best-first.","type":"boolean"},"max_body_bytes":{"description":"Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"memory_limit":{"description":"Memory hits to return; default 5. Half the slots (rounded up) are reserved for knowledge docs, annotations fill the rest, and either kind takes the other's unused slots.","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id or UUID.","type":["integer","string"]},"view":{"description":"How the TASK HALF is spelled. Default \"markdown\", the view YOU read; \"card\" is the D146 72-column box card in a text fence, for a PERSON deciding on the task (D164). Prerequisites and memory hits stay markdown.","enum":["markdown","card"],"type":"string"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_brief_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_summary"},"description":"Aggregate report grouped by project, status or priority. Pure read.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"all":{"description":"Count cancelled tasks too. By default a report with no status term skips cancelled only — done work always counts (D24).","type":"boolean"},"filter":{"description":"Optional filter DSL to scope the report.","type":"string"},"group_by":{"description":"Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.","enum":["project","status","priority"],"type":"string"},"metrics":{"description":"Extra columns per group. Omit and each group carries only `count`: every other metric is opt-in here, unlike `tasqx report`.","items":{"enum":["count","est_total","overdue","tracked_total","tokens_in","tokens_out","tokens_cache_read","tokens_cache_creation","tokens_unsplit"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"since":{"description":"Window `tracked_total` and the token buckets to spend at or after this instant, not the task's lifetime total — a different axis from `filter`'s `completed.*` terms (D97).","type":"string"},"until":{"description":"The other end of `since`: excludes anything at or after this instant. Together they window WHEN the spend happened.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_summary"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_outcomes"},"description":"How the work went rather than what it cost: rework, estimate calibration, token cost, unannotated completions, started-then-cancelled work, and `forced` (completions that overrode open blockers). Every rate carries the `n` it was computed over. Scope is tasks that CLOSED; `tasqx_summary` reads work in flight.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"filter":{"description":"Optional filter DSL to scope the report — `tasqx_list_tasks`' grammar.","type":"string"},"group_by":{"description":"Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.","enum":["project","status","priority"],"type":"string"},"metrics":{"description":"Which metrics to emit. Omit for ALL of them; naming none does not mean a bare count here.","items":{"enum":["rework","calibration","cost","silent","abandonment","overrun","unproven","forced"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"since":{"description":"Only count tasks that closed at or after this instant. `since`/`until` window WHEN THE TASK CLOSED, not when spend happened.","type":"string"},"until":{"description":"The other end of `since`: excludes tasks that closed at or after this instant.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_outcomes"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_list_projects"},"description":"List projects. By default excludes archived projects.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_archived":{"type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_list_projects"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_search_memory"},"description":"Search the memory store — imported docs and task annotations — bm25-ranked with snippets. A plain query is matched as phrases by word STEM and every word is REQUIRED, so `matched` explains a zero-hit answer; `raw: true` takes FTS5 syntax instead. A hit is an excerpt: `tasqx_get_memory` reads a doc whole, `tasqx_get_task` an annotation. `hits` is sorted best-first (LOWER bm25 `rank` is better); `total` and `has_more` say what `limit` cut. A doc hit adds `stale` (D180).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_rank":{"description":"Add the raw FTS5 bm25 `rank` to each hit. Default false. LOWER (more negative) is better and `hits` is already sorted best-first, so never use it as a threshold (D154).","type":"boolean"},"include_unscoped":{"description":"Widen a `project` scope to docs and annotations with NO project — what `tasqx memory import` produces. Never admits another project's. Refused without `project`.","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Max hits (0 or more); default 10. The response's `total`/`has_more` say what this left out.","type":"integer"},"project":{"description":"Scope to one project: docs stored with it, and annotations whose task carries it. Omit to search every project.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"Plain-text search words. Matched as quoted phrases, so hyphens and dots are safe.","type":"string"},"raw":{"description":"Pass the query through as FTS5 syntax. Invalid syntax is refused as bad_request.","type":"boolean"},"scope":{"description":"What to search. Optional; defaults to all.","enum":["all","docs","annotations"],"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_search_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_list_memory"},"description":"Browse memory docs without knowing a word inside one — what `tasqx_search_memory` cannot do without a query. Newest-modified first, paged like `tasqx_list_tasks`. A row is `id`, `title`, `source` and `modified`, enough to RECOGNISE a doc; `include_preview: true` adds the rest, and `tasqx_get_memory` reads one whole (D154).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_preview":{"description":"Return the whole engine row — `project`, `created`, `_rev`, a 160-character `body_preview`, `body_truncated` — instead of the four identifying fields. Default false (D154).","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Rows to return; default 20, because an unbounded browse page grows with the store.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"Matching docs to skip; pass the previous response's `next_offset`.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"project":{"description":"Restrict to docs stored with this `project`. Omit to list every doc.","type":"string"},"standing":{"description":"true lists only standing docs, false only the rest; omit for all (D156).","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_list_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_get_memory"},"description":"Read one knowledge doc whole, by the `id` a search hit carries — `tasqx_search_memory` returns only an excerpt. An annotation id is refused, naming the task to read it from instead.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"id":{"description":"The doc UUID, as a search hit or `tasqx_add_memory` prints it.","type":"string"}},"required":["id"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_get_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_add_task"},"description":"Create a task. Returns short_id, urgency and status — `backlog`, not `pending`, when `scheduled` or `wait` is in the future, which holds the task outside `@working` until then — plus the stored title, due, tags and resolved `scheduled`, so an ambiguous date or sugar captured into the title can be checked against what was stored. A title carrying CLI sugar adds a `warnings` entry naming it.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"budget_tokens":{"description":"Token budget (D139): a size gauge over FRESH tokens — input, output, cache creation, never cache reads. It STOPS NOTHING; a blown budget signals a task too big to hand over whole. `tasqx_get_task` reports `over` against it.","type":"integer"},"due":{"description":"The deadline; drives urgency and anchors relative reminders, and never hides the task. Date grammar: \"tomorrow\", \"friday\", \"2026-07-20\", \"in 3 days\", \"eom\", \"2026-07-20T17:00\" (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).","type":"string"},"estimate":{"description":"Duration: \"4h\", \"90m\", \"1h30m\", \"2d\", \"1w\", or ISO-8601 \"PT4H\".","type":"string"},"priority":{"description":"Priority: H (high), M (medium), or L (low).","enum":["H","M","L"],"type":"string"},"project":{"type":"string"},"recurrence":{"description":"Recurrence rule (D2 subset): \"daily\", \"every 3 days\", \"weekly on mon,wed\", \"monthly on day 15\", \"monthly on the last friday\".","type":"string"},"remind":{"description":"Reminder: a signed offset from `due` (\"-1h\", \"-30m\", \"-2d\", \"+15m\") or an absolute date in the `due` grammar.","type":"string"},"scheduled":{"description":"When you intend to start; a future value holds the task in `backlog` until it arrives. Date grammar: \"tomorrow\", \"friday\", \"2026-07-20\", \"in 3 days\", \"eom\", \"2026-07-20T17:00\" (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).","type":"string"},"tags":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"title":{"description":"Stored verbatim: this server does not parse the CLI's inline sugar (`+tag`, `project:`, `due:`, `!prio`). Use the fields below.","type":"string"},"wait":{"description":"Hides the task until then, in `backlog` like `scheduled` but meaning \"not my problem yet\". Date grammar: \"tomorrow\", \"friday\", \"2026-07-20\", \"in 3 days\", \"eom\", \"2026-07-20T17:00\" (bare clock = UTC; an offset is honoured).","type":"string"}},"required":["title"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_add_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_modify_task"},"description":"Change fields on a task via a `set` map. Returns `{short_id, _rev, set}`, where `set` echoes the RESOLVED value stored for each field named. Optimistic concurrency is ON: when `expected_rev` is omitted this server pins the task's current `_rev`, so a concurrent edit is a `conflict` naming both revs rather than a silent overwrite, and there is no way to opt out. On `conflict`, re-read the task, re-apply, retry (D75).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"expected_rev":{"description":"Optimistic-concurrency guard. Supplied by the server from the task's current `_rev` when omitted; pass it to pin a rev you read earlier. There is no last-writer-wins mode.","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"set":{"description":"Field → new value, e.g. {\"priority\":\"M\",\"due\":\"2026-07-22T17:00:00+02:00\"}.","type":"object"}},"required":["ref","set"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_modify_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_complete_task"},"description":"Mark a task done. Returns any tasks its completion newly unblocked. Report what this task cost via the *_tokens params, or `total_tokens` alone when you only know one number (D167): self-report is the primary channel, graded `medium` because nothing can check it (D50). `tool`/`model` are recorded on the event even with no count. A task with open dependencies is a `conflict` naming the blockers; `force: true` completes it anyway, counted by `tasqx_outcomes` (D150). `view: \"card\"` leads with the task's box card (D153), for a person deciding on it; a routine completion needs none (D164).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"cache_creation_tokens":{"description":"Self-reported cache-creation tokens (0 or more).","type":"integer"},"cache_read_tokens":{"description":"Self-reported cache-read tokens (0 or more).","type":"integer"},"checks_passed":{"description":"Ids of the acceptance criteria this work proved (D138). Completing with criteria open is not refused, but `tasqx_outcomes` counts it unproven.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"client":{"description":"Calling tool as \"<name> <version>\". Filled in from the MCP handshake when omitted.","type":"string"},"evidence":{"description":"One citation covering `checks_passed`: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha.","type":"string"},"force":{"description":"Complete despite still-open dependencies; without it that is a `conflict` naming them (D150). The override is recorded and counted under `forced`.","type":"boolean"},"input_tokens":{"description":"Self-reported input tokens (0 or more).","type":"integer"},"model":{"description":"The model doing the work, e.g. \"claude-opus-5\". Recorded with or without token counts.","type":"string"},"output_tokens":{"description":"Self-reported output tokens (0 or more).","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"session_id":{"description":"Your agent-session id, recorded on this task's event for token attribution.","type":"string"},"tool":{"description":"The AI tool doing the work, free-form (e.g. \"claude-code\"). Also names a token measurement, defaulting to `client`.","type":"string"},"total_tokens":{"description":"One unsplit count, instead of the four (D167).","type":"integer"},"transcript_path":{"description":"Absolute path to your session transcript, recorded on the same event.","type":"string"},"view":{"description":"Default \"markdown\": the plain JSON result. \"card\" leads with the D146 box card of the task AS COMPLETED, in a text fence, the JSON unchanged behind it, for a PERSON deciding on it (D164).","enum":["markdown","card"],"type":"string"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_complete_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_cancel_task"},"description":"Cancel a task: backlog, pending or active moves to cancelled. The row is kept and stops counting in reports. Returns the tasks the cancellation newly unblocked (D11: cancelling a blocker resolves it, like completing one). A task already closed is a conflict, not a no-op.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_cancel_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_reopen_task"},"description":"Reopen a closed task: done or cancelled goes back to pending, and the completion timestamp is cleared so the task stops counting in the week it is no longer finished in. A task that is not closed is a conflict, not a no-op.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_reopen_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_start_timer"},"description":"Start the timer on a task, moving it to active. The correlation params land on the start event for token attribution.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"actor":{"description":"Who is asking for the clock (D140); filled in with this connection's id when omitted. Starting while ANOTHER actor holds an active clock is a `conflict`, not a silent stop of their timer; pass `keep: true` to run both.","type":"string"},"client":{"description":"Calling tool as \"<name> <version>\". Filled in from the MCP handshake when omitted.","type":"string"},"include_memory":{"description":"Add `task.brief`'s memory search, 3 hits (D186). Default true; false answers the bare result.","type":"boolean"},"keep":{"description":"Keep other active tasks running (opt out of single-active).","type":"boolean"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"session_id":{"description":"Your agent-session id, recorded on this task's event for token attribution.","type":"string"},"transcript_path":{"description":"Absolute path to your session transcript, recorded on the same event.","type":"string"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_start_timer"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_stop_timer"},"description":"Stop the timer on a task. Returns `interval` (the duration just closed) and `tracked` (the task's running total, matching `tasqx_get_task`).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_stop_timer"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_adjust_tracked"},"description":"Correct tracked time by a signed `delta` (`-2h25m`, `+30m`); any status. `tasqx undo` reverts it.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"delta":{"description":"Signed duration: `-2h25m`, `+30m`.","type":"string"},"reason":{"description":"Why the time is corrected.","type":"string"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","delta","reason"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_adjust_tracked"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_tag_task"},"description":"Add one or more tags to a task. Tags are stored lowercase; one containing whitespace is refused. Returns the resulting tag set.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"tags":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["ref","tags"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_tag_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_untag_task"},"description":"Remove one or more tags from a task. Returns the resulting tag set. A tag the task does not carry is `not_found` and removes NONE of the tags named — all or nothing, so a typo can never answer ok.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"tags":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["ref","tags"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_untag_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_add_check"},"description":"Add an acceptance criterion to a task — one thing that must be true for it to count as done (D138). tasqx NEVER RUNS a check: it is a claim you mark later with evidence, not a command.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"body":{"description":"The criterion, in your own words. Stored verbatim.","type":"string"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","body"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_add_check"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_set_check"},"description":"Mark one acceptance criterion passed or failed, with the evidence for it. `failed` is a normal outcome worth recording. Evidence is stored verbatim and never interpreted.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"check_id":{"description":"The check's id, from `tasqx_get_task` or the add.","type":"string"},"evidence":{"description":"Your proof: a test name, an excerpt of output, a commit sha. Optional — an invented citation is worse than an unproven `passed`.","type":"string"},"position":{"description":"Or its 1-based place in tasqx_get_task's list.","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"state":{"description":"open | passed | failed.","enum":["open","passed","failed"],"type":"string"}},"required":["ref","state"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_set_check"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_remove_check"},"description":"Drop an acceptance criterion that turned out to be the wrong thing to ask. Use `tasqx_set_check` with `failed` when the criterion was right and the work did not meet it; deleting it would hide the finding.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"check_id":{"description":"The check's id.","type":"string"},"position":{"description":"Or its 1-based place in tasqx_get_task's list.","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_remove_check"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_annotate_task"},"description":"Attach a timestamped note to a task. The body is stored verbatim, newlines and markdown included, so long-form context lives here. The response echoes the body back as proof of that, or `{id, created, body_bytes}` under `include_body: false`. `tasqx_remove_annotation` on that `id` is the only way to take a note back.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"body":{"description":"Note text, stored verbatim. Multi-line markdown is fine.","type":"string"},"include_body":{"description":"Echo the stored body back. Default true (D72/D75): your proof the store kept it verbatim. Pass false for `body_bytes` in its place on a long note.","type":"boolean"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","body"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_annotate_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_add_tokens"},"description":"Record token spend on a task after the fact, e.g. a count that arrived after completion (D167). Send the split counts, or `total_tokens` alone when only one number is known — never both. Stored as a self-report at confidence `medium`, as on `tasqx_complete_task`: nothing can check it, so it is never `high` (D50); only a session-confirmed transcript or OTLP telemetry earns that. Reuse `idempotency_key` on a retry.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"cache_creation_tokens":{"type":"integer"},"cache_read_tokens":{"type":"integer"},"idempotency_key":{"description":"The same key twice on one task banks once.","type":"string"},"input_tokens":{"type":"integer"},"model":{"type":"string"},"output_tokens":{"type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"tool":{"description":"The AI tool that spent them; defaults to the handshake's client.","type":"string"},"total_tokens":{"description":"One unsplit count, instead of the four.","type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_add_tokens"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_remove_annotation"},"description":"Permanently scrub one annotation's text by id. Unlike every other write here this is a HARD delete: the body is overwritten in the store and the original `annotation.add` event's body is redacted in the same transaction, so a secret is gone from `event.list` and `store.export` too (D113). A text-free tombstone stays for audit under `annotations_removed`. `tasqx undo` does NOT cover this. An unknown or removed id is `not_found`.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"annotation_id":{"description":"The annotation's id, as tasqx_annotate_task or tasqx_get_task reports.","type":"string"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","annotation_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_remove_annotation"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_update_annotation"},"description":"Correct one annotation's body in place, by id (D165): id, timestamp and position are kept, and search stops finding the old text. `tasqx undo` covers it. An omitted `expected_rev` pins the task's current `_rev`, as on `tasqx_modify_task`.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"annotation_id":{"description":"The annotation's id, as tasqx_annotate_task or tasqx_get_task reports.","type":"string"},"body":{"description":"The corrected text; replaces the old body whole.","type":"string"},"expected_rev":{"description":"Guard on the task's `_rev`; supplied by the server when omitted.","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","annotation_id","body"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_update_annotation"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_add_dependency"},"description":"Make one task depend on another: `ref` is blocked until `depends_on` is done or cancelled, and a `ref` already closed is never blocked. Returns the resulting dependency list and blocked state. A cycle is refused as a conflict.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"depends_on":{"description":"The task `ref` must wait for: short_id or UUID.","type":["integer","string"]},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","depends_on"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_add_dependency"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_remove_dependency"},"description":"Cut a dependency edge: `ref` stops waiting on `depends_on`. Returns the remaining dependency list and blocked state, so the answer says whether the task is actionable now or still waiting on something else.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"depends_on":{"description":"The blocker to stop waiting for: short_id or UUID.","type":["integer","string"]},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["ref","depends_on"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_remove_dependency"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_add_memory"},"description":"Store a knowledge document in memory: patterns, documentation, decisions worth finding again. The body is stored verbatim (markdown fine) and becomes searchable through tasqx_search_memory.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"body":{"description":"Stored verbatim; multi-line markdown is fine.","type":"string"},"project":{"description":"Optional project scope. Omit to leave the doc unscoped; it is never defaulted onto a current project.","type":"string"},"source":{"description":"Where this came from: a path, URL, or ticket. One doc per source: one another doc holds is a `conflict` naming it (D174).","type":"string"},"standing":{"description":"True marks a ruling that belongs in every session of its scope until retracted; default false (D156).","type":"boolean"},"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["title","body"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_add_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_update_memory"},"description":"Correct a memory doc in place — title, body, source and/or project — by id. Prefer it over a second `tasqx_add_memory`: a correction written as a new doc leaves the stale one polluting search rankings, and `tasqx_remove_memory` is permanent. Optimistic concurrency as on `tasqx_modify_task`: an omitted `expected_rev` pins the current `rev`, so a concurrent edit is a `conflict` naming both (D75).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"body":{"description":"New body, stored verbatim. Omit to leave unchanged.","type":"string"},"expected_rev":{"description":"Optimistic-concurrency guard. Supplied by the server from the doc's current `rev` when omitted; pass it to pin a rev you read earlier.","type":"integer"},"id":{"description":"The doc UUID, as a search hit, `tasqx_add_memory` or `tasqx_list_memory` prints it.","type":"string"},"project":{"description":"New project scope. Omit to leave unchanged.","type":"string"},"source":{"description":"New source. Omit to leave unchanged. One another doc holds is a `conflict` naming it (D174).","type":"string"},"standing":{"description":"Set or clear the standing flag; omit to leave unchanged (D156).","type":"boolean"},"title":{"description":"New title. Omit to leave unchanged.","type":"string"}},"required":["id"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_update_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_remove_memory"},"description":"Remove one knowledge document from memory by id. Use it to retract something that turned out wrong: a correction written as a second document leaves both in the store, with search ranking them together. The removal is permanent — `tasqx undo` does not cover memory docs, and the body is not recoverable from the event log.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"id":{"description":"The document's id, as tasqx_search_memory reports it on a `doc` hit.","type":"string"}},"required":["id"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_remove_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"tasqx_create_project"},"description":"Create a project. Returns its id and name. It does NOT become the default project — MCP exposes no `project.use` (D22) — so pass `project` explicitly on every `tasqx_add_task` that should land here.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"description":{"type":"string"},"name":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_create_project"}]}}
